      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This seems to only apply to custom shaders.\nAttached are comparisons between two materials being blocked.\nWhen using the built-in Unity Standard shader, only the alpha of the lens is is lost due to the incorrect rendering mode applied (transparent to opaque). Though when using a custom shader, the missing maps include emission, metallic/roughness, alpha and ambient occlusion.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
